{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted","id":87572,"title":"Sidereal as the 0 Resistance/Stamina Exalted ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-09T10:39:50-07:00","id":87572,"title":"Sidereal as the 0 Resistance/Stamina Exalted ?","content":"Ox-Body Technique is such a weak and horrible charm, and some people seem to think that Sidereal has the worst OBT among the splat, so they go make thread about how awful Sid's OBT is, and there seem to be some respond that keep popping up:<ul><li>Sidereal are Martial Artist Exalted, Martial Artist in some Wuxia movie that I watch never got hit =&gt; Sidereal must be squishy.</li> <li>Sidereal are Ninja Exalt, Ninja are squishy in other game =&gt; Sidereal are squishy.</li> <li>Sidereal are Bureaucrat Exalted, bureaucrat manipulate from the shadow and not on the front =&gt; Every Sidereal are squishy because they don't need Resistance.</li> <li>Sidereal have powerful charms and high offensive powers =&gt; They must be balanced by making them squishy.</li> <li>Doctor Moran comment about the Sidereal &quot;I expect that Sidereals would train intensively for years, direct Dragon-Blooded and advise Solars in a handful of battles, and then for one reason or another they'd have to actually go out and fight, and they would <u>die</u>.&quot; =&gt; Sidereal are squishy.</li> </ul><br /> So I guess the purpose of this thread is to ask whether Sidereal charmset be crippled mechanically to enforce the aesthetic of &quot;Glass Canon Stripper Tea-cup Ninja&quot; ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 05-26-2014, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:08:16-07:00","id":87585,"title":"","content":"I think of Sidereals like Brainiac. Brainiac is the smartest sentient being in the DC universe, with fucktons of knowledge and self-built infrastructure and the best plans and blah blah blah, but he still loses against Superman every time because intelligence and planning and infrastructure are not enough if you don't have personal power to back it up. Solars, like Superman, have personal power.<br /> <br /> It's a statement not just about Sidereals, but the nature of the world that is Creation: power wins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:11:45-07:00","id":87592,"title":"","content":"Sidereal Ox-Body exists specifically to do one job, help cover the cost of all the Sid charms that cost Health Levels to use.<br /> <br /> Though I have seen some builds that use Sid Ox-Body to make the Sid appear to be invincible, they are definitely the the exception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:14:46-07:00","id":87596,"title":"","content":"OX body is great for Sidereals, It gives them more motes!<br /> <br /> :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2438-satori","name":"Satori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:14:48-07:00","id":87597,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression that Sidereals were the splat intended for people who wanted to play &quot;the man behind the man&quot;. As a general rule, the man behind the man do not and should not place themselves in situations where they need to rely on toughness or personal fortitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:24:01-07:00","id":87607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87597#post87597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that Sidereals were the splat intended for people who wanted to play &quot;the man behind the man&quot;. As a general rule, the man behind the man do not and should not place themselves in situations where they need to rely on toughness or personal fortitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every Sidereal is Ketchup Carjack sitting on his chair manipulating his minion. Iron Siaka just pound demon's faces directly instead of making other people do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87592#post87592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereal Ox-Body exists specifically to do one job, help cover the cost of all the Sid charms that cost Health Levels to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, shouldn't that mean they ought to get more HL per purchase instead of a single -0 level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 03-09-2014, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:34:52-07:00","id":87613,"title":"","content":"Sure, there are situations where you need to jump someone and gank them in order to maintain your plan, but as a general rule Sidereal themeatics are much like Fate, sneaky, subtle and manipulative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:45:09-07:00","id":87620,"title":"","content":"I don't really care for splat &quot;thematic&quot; and stereotype so my question is quite simple: &quot;Will Sidereal have weaker combat/soak charm than other Exalted in order to play up the image of shadow behind the throne&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:51:53-07:00","id":87624,"title":"","content":"Sidereals are characters that are being played by players. This tautology must be remembered and understood.<br /> <br /> Sidereals as subtle behind-the-scenes-manipulators who die when they enter a fight does not allow player to engage the system in its epic wuxia kung fu features, which are a big appeal of Exalted as a whole and Sidereals in particular, what with their focus on mystical martial arts.<br /> <br /> Sidereals who die when they have to fight are bad design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:52:48-07:00","id":87627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87620#post87620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really care for splat &quot;thematic&quot; and stereotype so my question is quite simple: &quot;Will Sidereal have weaker combat/soak charm than other Exalted in order to play up the image of shadow behind the throne&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Resistance 5 Sidereal with the Scripture of the Eternal Maiden floating in the air above her head is not going to get randomly shafted because the Sidereals draw thematically from secret agents and ninjas, no. Sidereal Resistance probably won't work quite the same way as Solar Resistance or Lunar Stamina, but that is hardly anything new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:55:07-07:00","id":87630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87597#post87597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that Sidereals were the splat intended for people who wanted to play &quot;the man behind the man&quot;. As a general rule, the man behind the man do not and should not place themselves in situations where they need to rely on toughness or personal fortitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the theory. The problem with this is that this is fine for NPCs, but it's pure and simple not how actual games go. You can't design a player splat under the assumption that plans will go smoothly and when they don't and the man behind the man is forced into the light he crumples up like old tissue paper - because that area where plans NEVER go smoothly and people live in interesting times and have to frequently fight for their lives is where PCs <i>live </i>almost all of their screen time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:57:28-07:00","id":87633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87620#post87620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really care for splat &quot;thematic&quot; and stereotype so my question is quite simple: &quot;Will Sidereal have weaker combat/soak charm than other Exalted in order to play up the image of shadow behind the throne&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course Sidereals will have some combat Charms that are weaker than those of other Exalted. No doubt they will also have some that are stronger. This is entirely in keeping with previous editions. <br /> <br /> Trying to judge the combat-worthyness of an entire group based on the relative strength of a Charm you think is horrible and worthless in all it's incarnations seems ... odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T12:18:53-07:00","id":87650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87624#post87624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals who die when they have to fight are bad design.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but die to whom? Iron Siaka makes first circle demons look like punks, and at least according to the fiction, she handles second circles without dying. She'd spank a Dragon-Blood up and down the street. I think it might be worth pointing out that squishiness is relative, and if Sidereals are only squishy to things like Solaroids, third circle demons, and shit in that general power range, then they're still way less squishy than most of the rest of the world; and if they're only at a significant disadvantage to the world-defining powers, then that just means it's more heroic when they use the resources they have to fight those threats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T12:38:08-07:00","id":87665,"title":"","content":"Sidereals are comparatively fragile and brittle, but this tends to express itself in a variety of ways. Probably the easiest way to see it is to look at the idea behind SMA (even if the implementations have generally had issues): SMA is really powerful, but that power depends on a specific strategy or approach. You are really great at fighting -- as long as your &quot;trick&quot; keeps working. If you get knocked out of your game, you're often screwed.<br /> <br /> Whereas, say, Solar or Lunar combat styles don't work that way; the best Lunar tricks are generally not going to have anything as strong as a SMA style fighting on its terms with ever cylinder firing, but they will tend to be more broadly applicable and reliable.<br /> <br /> Sidereals aren't bad fighters, but they are best at fighting <i>like a Sidereal</i>, which usually means planning ahead, relying on tricks and manipulation -- even in a fight -- and so on. This tends to mean that if you screw up, you have less room for error. It also means that there tends to be rules and limitations you have to worry about, which will cause problems for you (including failures in combat) if you don't cover for them.<br /> <br /> Sidereal combat styles also tend to be a bit risk-averse (as opposed to, say, Lunars, who can probably afford to take risks because they have more health levels and can get them back easier.) The idea is that Sidereals don't flip a coin unless they've weighted it in advance.<br /> <br /> Whereas if you want to be able to drop everything with no warning or plan and lunge at someone's throat while howling for blood, or if you want combat styles that will almost always work reasonably well, Lunars or Solars are a better bet.<br /> <br /> Sidereals having fewer motes and health levels in general is part of this because those things give you more margin for error, which allows you to play it by ear -- that's something that Sidereals are generally worse at than other Exalted. But that doesn't mean that they're bad at combat, it means that they're bad at a style of combat where you take risks and rely on your ability to soak up hits to cover for mistakes.<br /> <br /> Of course this is just generalities -- Sidereals are still capable of fighting with no plan when they have to, and they have to sometimes be able to take a hit. But it's a bad strategy for them. The idea behind Avoidance Kata and their future-warning charms isn't to never fight ever, but to make sure you fight on your own terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T13:27:28-07:00","id":87694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted#post87572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ox-Body Technique is such a weak and horrible charm, and some people seem to think that Sidereal has the worst OBT among the splat, so they go make thread about how aweful Sid's OBT is</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's because I lack sufficient experience in Exalted combat, but I don't agree with any part of this. Exalted is not a JRPG or an MMO where you expect to get hit every time the enemy attacks. It's a game about heroes who fight cinematically, which means they don't often get hit, and when they do, they don't usually take serious damage. Ox-Body allows you to reflect the punishment you can endure, but Resistance Charms and armor are what allow you to not take serious punishment in the first place.<br /> <br /> Ox-Body -0 is for characters who take a punch or a gash and don't even flinch. When your health levels come from Ox-Body -0, you end up looking like the Terminator. Bullet holes? Who cares.<br /> <br /> Ox-Body 2x-1 is for characters who can take a serious beating and stay in the fight. Your character shows that they are human, they feel pain, and they can be slowed down, but they don't give up. The synergy with Battle Fury Focus is intentional.<br /> <br /> Ox-Body -1, 2x-2 is for characters who <i>just won't die</i>. This is for Rocky characters. You see them get seriously messed up, but they stay in the fight against all odds or sense.<br /> <br /> Sidereals only have access to Ox-Body -0 not because they are fragile, but because the way in which they are durable is the way the Terminator is durable: damage doesn't slow them down at all until it gets really serious. Lunars have access to 4x-2 because they are the monsters who keep fighting in spite of grievous injury. Solars have access to a broad set of Ox-Body options because some of them are Terminators and some of them are Rockys, and some of them are something in between.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T13:50:59-07:00","id":87710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted#post87572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Doctor Moran comment about the Sidereal &quot;I expect that Sidereals would train intensively for years, direct Dragon-Blooded and advise Solars in a handful of battles, and then for one reason or another they'd have to actually go out and fight, and they would <u>die</u>.&quot; =&gt; Sidereal are squishy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that this was specifically in regards to fighting in the Primordial War against primordials, and at that point Sidereal Martial arts were not a thing. Plus the situation was set up to be very stacked against the Sidereal.<br /> <br /> Still, it's a slightly annoying quote largely because Sidereals aren't really the best at directing/Teaching: those roles seem to be better fulfilled by Solars in 2ed.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87694#post87694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe it's because I lack sufficient experience in Exalted combat, but I don't agree with any part of this. Exalted is not a JRPG or an MMO where you expect to get hit every time the enemy attacks. It's a game about heroes who fight cinematically, which means they don't often get hit, and when they do, they don't usually take serious damage. Ox-Body allows you to reflect the punishment you can endure, but Resistance Charms and armor are what allow you to not take serious punishment in the first place.<br /> <br /> Ox-Body -0 is for characters who take a punch or a gash and don't even flinch. When your health levels come from Ox-Body -0, you end up looking like the Terminator. Bullet holes? Who cares.<br /> <br /> Ox-Body 2x-1 is for characters who can take a serious beating and stay in the fight. Your character shows that they are human, they feel pain, and they can be slowed down, but they don't give up. The synergy with Battle Fury Focus is intentional.<br /> <br /> Ox-Body -1, 2x-2 is for characters who <i>just won't die</i>. This is for Rocky characters. You see them get seriously messed up, but they stay in the fight against all odds or sense.<br /> <br /> Sidereals only have access to Ox-Body -0 not because they are fragile, but because the way in which they are durable is the way the Terminator is durable: damage doesn't slow them down at all until it gets really serious. Lunars have access to 4x-2 because they are the monsters who keep fighting in spite of grievous injury. Solars have access to a broad set of Ox-Body options because some of them are Terminators and some of them are Rockys, and some of them are something in between.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how it worked, due to the wound penalties. Those meant that either all you really cared about level 0(and maybe level -1), or you had a wound penalty negator, in which case for combat, all your wounds were -0, in which case the options that gave you the most health levels were the best. Especially since damage was generally high for most of 2nd, which meant that you needed the largest number of health levels in order to survive a couple hits.<br /> <br /> Now, this is already not good for Sidereals, but it's worse because Sidereal charms often have health level costs, and since you only get one health level per Ox Body, it means that those charms often essentially cost double for them to even be usable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T14:24:49-07:00","id":87728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87607#post87607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, shouldn't that mean they ought to get more HL per purchase instead of a single -0 level.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the point is that you are not suffering a wound penalty for using those charms that cost a HL. Also most of the charms are scene length so you aren't going to be reactivating them. Sidereal charms are indirect in their power and Sid Ox-Body is no different. Instead of making you tougher by being able to take lots of damage, Sid Ox Body makes you tougher by making it easier to use the most powerful charms the in the Sid tool box.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T14:43:20-07:00","id":87743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoSaR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87710#post87710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, it's a slightly annoying quote largely because Sidereals aren't really the best at directing/Teaching: those roles seem to be better fulfilled by Solars in 2ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>To a point, I'd say this is more a symptom of the following kind of thinking: &quot;Do you have the best Charm for X? No? Then you are not the best at X.&quot; And not having a Charm for X at all means you suck at it. Having a Charm that expresses your incredible skill at directing/teaching means that you have incredible skill at directing/teaching and nothing more. This is a very important distinction: it means that what you have skillfully directed or taught people to do could in fact have been an unbelievably terrible thing to direct/teach them to do. An adviser in this context is more the type of person who would be good at directing someone toward or teaching someone what a good/better thing to direct/teach would be.<br /> <br /> It's an open question of how well it worked (I'm not familiar enough to say), but Sidereals have a number of powers that make them very good at gathering the kind of info someone would want or need before making decisions to carry a task out with extreme confidence like that. Google Spider is the most memorable, but it's also worth remembering that this is the splat that can see the future. It's... sort of hard to overstate the value of that last one in an adviser in concept, regardless of how well the concept was executed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T15:03:28-07:00","id":87759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87592#post87592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereal Ox-Body exists specifically to do one job, help cover the cost of all the Sid charms that cost Health Levels to use.<br /> <br /> Though I have seen some builds that use Sid Ox-Body to make the Sid appear to be invincible, they are definitely the the exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it doesn't do it well though. For what you are paying it doesn't provide anything. Even if you need health levels in 3e paying 9-11xp for just one is bullshit. They need to get something with it. Whether it's TN modifying effects or converting -1,2, or 4 health levels to 0 as well. One health level regardless of circumstance is awful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 03-09-2014, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T15:28:45-07:00","id":87772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87759#post87759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it doesn't do it well though. For what you are paying it doesn't provide anything. Even if you need health levels in 3e paying 9-11xp for just one is bullshit. They need to get something with it. Whether it's TN modifying effects or converting -1,2, or 4 health levels to 0 as well. One health level regardless of circumstance is awful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm definitely inclined to agree that it should likely do more, but I'd also note we don't know the context yet, both of Sidereals and the broader EX3 combat system. I mean, part of the issue was that even the better Ox-Bodies (across splats) still weren't very good because of how combat worked. According to playtester feedback, Solar Ox-Body is now <i>desirable</i> in the new paradigm.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, still agreeing in general that I'd like to see more from it than just the 1 health level, but I'd be interested to see how it would fly in context of the rest of EX3 before I'd call it unquestionably terrible.<br /> <br /> On a tangential note, I don't think there's been any discussion of differing XP costs for different splats. I shall hope the concept -- at least and especially regarding Charms -- has been shot 108 times in the head, drawn and quartered, and those pieces carried in locked boxes to be hidden in the distant corners of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T15:38:11-07:00","id":87777,"title":"","content":"Back in 2E, I played Sidereal Ox-Body as giving two -0 Levels. That makes it strictly better than the DB OBT, but then, so is the Solar one. I felt like that let Sidereals keep their &quot;seemingly invulnerable but actually fragile&quot; status while not nerfing them quite as deep into oblivion.<br /> <br /> Which is really the answer to this issue as a whole, I think. In 2E, everyone's Ox-Body was secretly useless, but the Sidereals managed to have the worst Perfects of any Celestial, so they were in deep trouble. In 2.5, their Perfects got a little better, but Health Levels mattered... and worse, armor mattered, and many of the best Martial Arts (such as their signature Violet Bier Of Sorrows Style) didn't allow it. In both cases, the issue wasn't so much that being a glass canon is unplayable or even overly limiting - it's that <i>everyone</i> was a canon, but the Sidereals alone had to pay for it by being glass.<br /> <br /> As ever, I can only express amusement and confusion at people trying to turn this into a mechanical complain against a system which is not yet released, but I don't think it's impossible to make &quot;brittle strength&quot; a Sidereal thematic while still (1) letting them be viable combatants, and (2) giving them space for a variety of designs and niches, combat and otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T15:39:09-07:00","id":87778,"title":"","content":"It does it perfectly well. Are you seriously trying to get up more than 6 Prayer Strip charms at one time? Most characters will never even have that many Prayer strip charms.<br /> <br /> One -0 HL is pathetic if the point of that health level is to absorb damage, but that isn't the point. The point of that -0 HL is to avoid suffering wound penalties as a result of activating your most powerful charms, and that since -0 HL does that fantastically. No Sidereal charm should be viewed in isolation from the rest of the charmset, the intent is that they all weave together synergistically. <br /> <br /> If the charm instead said that you could could activate and maintain one charm that costs a single health level to activate without first paying the health level, and could be repurchased up to 5 times allowing you to maintain five charms with HL costs without paying a single health level it would be praised as awesome despite the fact that the charm would be substantially less powerful that the current sidereal ox-body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T16:43:37-07:00","id":87803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87743#post87743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To a point, I'd say this is more a symptom of the following kind of thinking: &quot;Do you have the best Charm for X? No? Then you are not the best at X.&quot; And not having a Charm for X at all means you suck at it. Having a Charm that expresses your incredible skill at directing/teaching means that you have incredible skill at directing/teaching and nothing more. This is a very important distinction: it means that what you have skillfully directed or taught people to do could in fact have been an unbelievably terrible thing to direct/teach them to do. An adviser in this context is more the type of person who would be good at directing someone toward or teaching someone what a good/better thing to direct/teach would be.<br /> <br /> It's an open question of how well it worked (I'm not familiar enough to say), but Sidereals have a number of powers that make them very good at gathering the kind of info someone would want or need before making decisions to carry a task out with extreme confidence like that. Google Spider is the most memorable, but it's also worth remembering that this is the splat that can see the future. It's... sort of hard to overstate the value of that last one in an adviser in concept, regardless of how well the concept was executed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that a major component working against Sid's(at least in second edition up to a certain point) was that they couldn't see out of fate things, and that 2 second circle and up things are out of fate by their nature...yeah, that didn't work well. Which is why I brought it up. Because I'm not, in fact, an idiot.<br /> <br /> It is interesting that your argument is basically &quot;&quot;Sidereals are the best at directing because while they don't have the best abilities regarding those areas, they have the best abilities regarding those areas.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's also somewhat annoying because it plays into the stupid idea that 2 of the Sidereal castes, and a large part of their inspirations, are actually traps, and that Sidereals should not get involved in combat at all(this is an actual argument I have been involved in).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87728#post87728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the point is that you are not suffering a wound penalty for using those charms that cost a HL. Also most of the charms are scene length so you aren't going to be reactivating them. Sidereal charms are indirect in their power and Sid Ox-Body is no different. Instead of making you tougher by being able to take lots of damage, Sid Ox Body makes you tougher by making it easier to use the most powerful charms the in the Sid tool box.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but no part of a system should be viewed in isolation, and the fact that Sidereals have no means to boost their health levels(by your admission) that aren't terrible is something of a problem, at least when health levels are somewhat relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T17:34:35-07:00","id":87821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoSaR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87803#post87803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, but no part of a system should be viewed in isolation, and the fact that Sidereals have no means to boost their health levels(by your admission) that aren't terrible is something of a problem, at least when health levels are somewhat relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've again missed the point of Sidereals in that that do not deal with damage in the form of health levels. That would be far to straight forward for Sidereals. The Sidereals approach is far less direct using things like Shield of Destiny to extend their effective health track, and a wide array of far less direct techniques.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T17:51:03-07:00","id":87832,"title":"","content":"Given that, at least in 2.5e, Sidereals have incredibly easy access to a wound penalty negator, getting -0s compared to any other type of health level in larger amounts isn't really any benefit.<br /> <br /> But really, extra health levels in 2e Exalted are pretty useless without large numbers of them, making an entire Charm purchase gaining a single -0 pretty ridiculous. It's really a hold-over of old design; Solars had the option of gaining one -0, mind you, and that was supposed to be equivalent to two -1s or one -1/two -2s. By that notion, the Sidereal OBT is effectively Solar-level in power, though more limited. This also served to show how -0s were useful to Sidereals for prayer strips and to show them as the untouchable ninjas that even when hit didn't get <i>wounded.</i> But as it turns out, that design notion didn't hold up, making Sids' OBT just plain bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T17:58:59-07:00","id":87840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87832#post87832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that, at least in 2.5e, Sidereals have incredibly easy access to a wound penalty negator, getting -0s compared to any other type of health level in larger amounts isn't really any benefit.<br /> <br /> But really, extra health levels in 2e Exalted are pretty useless without large numbers of them, making an entire Charm purchase gaining a single -0 pretty ridiculous. It's really a hold-over of old design; Solars had the option of gaining one -0, mind you, and that was supposed to be equivalent to two -1s or one -1/two -2s. By that notion, the Sidereal OBT is effectively Solar-level in power, though more limited. This also served to show how -0s were useful to Sidereals for prayer strips and to show them as the untouchable ninjas that even when hit didn't get <i>wounded.</i> But as it turns out, that design notion didn't hold up, making Sids' OBT just plain bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel it is worth noting that in a world without wound-penalty negators, the -0 option is actually really good. The math has been done before to show that someone with 5 -0 Ox-Bodies have a good chance of winning against someone with 5x -1/-2/-2 in an even fight solely because wound penalties are that big of a deal. However the design breaks completely the moment wound-penalty negators enter the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T18:10:39-07:00","id":87842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87821#post87821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've again missed the point of Sidereals in that that do not deal with damage in the form of health levels. That would be far to straight forward for Sidereals. The Sidereals approach is far less direct using things like Shield of Destiny to extend their effective health track, and a wide array of far less direct techniques.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm not missing the point: soak helps, but it is not a replacement for health levels. Especially when one effect has no active cost, and the other costs at minimum 3m, 1wp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T18:15:55-07:00","id":87844,"title":"","content":"Given the changes to Resistance in 2.5, I would expect to see a set-up along the lines of this:<br /> <br /> Sidereals who choose to invest in Resistance <i>can</i> be tough targets- although it's important to remember that Sidereal Resistance is a much more offensive fuck-you style of Resistance than Solars do- but they're not passively so. You must take time to activate your charms in order to become tough. This fits rather well with the general Sidereal weakness of being bad at improvising; if a Sidereal wants to defeat someone, they ambush. If you want to defeat a Sidereal, <i>you</i> should ambush.*<br /> <br /> The lack of armor is (<b>I</b> think) sad as an aesthetic thing, but Sidereal Resistance provides you bonuses for not having it anyway. I think that if a Sidereal warrior jumps you, Form up, katas at the ready, practically buzzing with defensive destiny, you could easily waste a quiver of arrows. If you decide to duel the Sidereal in the hallway, those arrows will probably go right in, except for the part where the Sidereal vanishes and you catch yourself wondering why you were shooting arrows into that fresco.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Mind you, between Awareness and Avoidance Kata, someone seeking to ambush a Sidereal must do a lot better than lying in wait at night somewhere. A prepared and powerful Sidereal's weakness has always been a fight which he didn't see coming but can't afford to lose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T18:19:21-07:00","id":87845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoSaR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87842#post87842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm not missing the point: soak helps, but it is not a replacement for health levels. Especially when one effect has no active cost, and the other costs at minimum 3m, 1wp.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mention any soak charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T19:17:24-07:00","id":87872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87845#post87845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't mention any soak charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny, the charm you mentioned is a step-7 raw damage reducer that can't reduce things past 1 die of damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T21:27:35-07:00","id":87930,"title":"","content":"Sidereal are Wizards and only get to start with 1d4 HP and no ability to wear anything other than a dress.<br /> <br /> Sorry. :/<br /> <br /> But you have access to the best dressmakers in the setting! \\o/<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87844#post87844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to defeat a Sidereal, <i>you</i> should ambush.*<br /> <br /> *Mind you, between Awareness and Avoidance Kata, someone seeking to ambush a Sidereal must do a lot better than lying in wait at night somewhere. A prepared and powerful Sidereal's weakness has always been a fight which he didn't see coming but can't afford to lose.</div> </div> </div> </div>My housecat as killed so many young Sidereals by running through their feet unexpectedly, causing them to trip and fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-10-2014, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T22:16:41-07:00","id":87966,"title":"","content":"The purpose of Sidereal Ox-Body is to point out that Paradox actually isn't shit, because you only have to take SOB four times before you won't get killed for using your own powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T22:40:05-07:00","id":87979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87930#post87930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My housecat as killed so many young Sidereals by running through their feet unexpectedly, causing them to trip and fall.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose you could say that they should have asked the Maidens for... (Sunglasses) Avoidance Cat-a.<br /> <br /> [YEAHHHHHHH!!]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T01:56:18-07:00","id":88030,"title":"","content":"Saur ops Specialist, you are my hero.<br /> <br /> I am breaking my vows of celibacy just to have a firstborn child, which I will then name after you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T02:27:46-07:00","id":149239,"title":"","content":"true sid's OBT sounds really disappointing (especially the lack of choice more than in the fact that it's -0)<br /> <br /> On the other hand I read a lot on interesting explanations I didn't think of for why it was made this way.<br /> <br /> To contribute to the subject, in the games I play in a house-rule changed the charm so that for every purchase you also convert one heal level into another health level with a penalty 1 lower, starting with the one that has the lowest penalty.<br /> <br /> To clarify : when you buy you'r 1st ox-body, you het a -0 HL and you convert a -1 HL into a -0.<br /> The second purchase would convert the second -1 into a -0.<br /> The third and fourh would respectively convert one fo your -2 into -1 and then -0.<br /> <br /> The end result with 10 OBT (the max you can buy) is a sid with 16 -0 and then directly falls into incapacitated. Help them because they have few choices for ignoring wound penalties, which was quite limited (either constantly pump motes in excellencies, or costly charms like heartless maiden trance)<br /> <br /> This was inspired by the fact that lunars have a &quot;bonus&quot; on their OBT that fits their style (dying HLs IIRC) that doesn't totally change the math of health level acquisition. And you could probably think of another theme bonus for other splats if you think they get disadvantaged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T06:44:21-07:00","id":149362,"title":"","content":"I guess my question is, &quot;What is this thread <i>even</i>?&quot;<br /> <br /> Sidereals don't get to pick their OBT; neither do a bunch of other splats, so they're hardly alone in that; additionally, their Resistance tree is not limited to Ox-Bodies. 2.5 in particular really made Sidereal Resistance stand out, and I'd like to see what the devs do for Sidereals before any of us try and take torches and pitchforks to it, please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-26-2014, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T07:17:09-07:00","id":149382,"title":"","content":"Sidereals are over powered imo anyway...<br /> <br /> They never got decimated like the solars &amp; lunars did...<br /> When they exalt they get a job in heaven with benefits...<br /> They have the most powerful martial arts...<br /> The crap they can do with fate is just weird, confusing and nasty...<br /> They have access to way more divine backing than any other kind of exalt period...<br /> They have their freaky little hands in everyone's cookie jar...<br /> They get trainers and have a easier time at life period compared to other celestial exalts...<br /> <br /> &amp; my ST loves them to death and they are usually the powers that be in some of his games<br /> and end up fuckin with me and mine and i cant remember who it was because of their screwy<br /> memory thingy thing... you ever want to kick someones ass but didnt know who's &amp; even if you<br /> did they just break out prismatic arrangement of creation style and 50 form charms at once...<br /> and your like... dude i am essence 2!!!! I exalted like 3 weeks ago... stop picking on me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you think nobody cares if you're alive, try missing a couple of payments.","edited":{"userid":2890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2890-walker-of-ebony-clouds","user":"Walker-of-Ebony-Clouds","date":". 05-26-2014, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2890-walker-of-ebony-clouds","name":"Walker-of-Ebony-Clouds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T11:02:02-07:00","id":149553,"title":"","content":"Part of the issue here is one of contrast. Sidereals are not squishy compared to mortals. Playing a big, buff sid who can take a bunch of blows is fine.<br /> <br /> However, if you're comparing Sidereals to Lunars, who can become turtle godzillas, they'll be squishy in comparison. Likewise, Solars, Abyssals, and Infernals each get to draw on superhuman stamina because there are mythic heroes who can never be budged or broken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87979#post87979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose you could say that they should have asked the Maidens for... (Sunglasses) Avoidance Cat-a.<br /> <br /> [YEAHHHHHHH!!]</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad someone bumped this thread just so I could see this pun again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 05-26-2014, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T15:55:11-07:00","id":149767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walker-of-Ebony-Clouds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=149382#post149382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals are over powered imo anyway...<br /> <br /> They never got decimated like the solars &amp; lunars did...</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't count the casualties they suffered during the Usurpation, the Balorian Crusade and the Great Contagion, sure! But if you do, then you'll see they tend to lose large numbers of their (already tiny) faction on a horribly consistent basis. And that's not counting the more standard deaths from, you know, living in Creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When they exalt they get a job in heaven with benefits...<br /> They have the most powerful martial arts...<br /> The crap they can do with fate is just weird, confusing and nasty...<br /> They have access to way more divine backing than any other kind of exalt period...<br /> They have their freaky little hands in everyone's cookie jar...<br /> They get trainers and have a easier time at life period compared to other celestial exalts... </div> </div> </div>And they're duty bound to Heaven, and they're constantly monitored and audited by petty gods that consider them pawns in Celestial politics, and they're horribly overworked, and they have murderous inter-factional politics, and their lives are constantly on the line, and they can't make any friends outside of the Five-Score Fellowship...<br /> <br /> In other words, being a Sidereal comes with a lot of perks, but the downsides are pretty shitty too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &amp; my ST loves them to death and they are usually the powers that be in some of his games<br /> and end up fuckin with me and mine and i cant remember who it was because of their screwy<br /> memory thingy thing... you ever want to kick someones ass but didnt know who's &amp; even if you<br /> did they just break out prismatic arrangement of creation style and 50 form charms at once...<br /> and your like... dude i am essence 2!!!! I exalted like 3 weeks ago... stop picking on me! </div> </div> </div>This sounds less like it's a problem with Sidereals (who logically wouldn't be spending all their time trolling your character because they have other shit to do) and more to do with a vindictive and petty ST. Have you considered talking to him about your frustrations on this matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T17:40:45-07:00","id":149867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=149767#post149767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds less like it's a problem with Sidereals (who logically wouldn't be spending all their time trolling your character because they have other shit to do) and more to do with a vindictive and petty ST. Have you considered talking to him about your frustrations on this matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea no kidding, our ST horribly misrepresents them &amp; we actually house ruled it that he cannot use them in our games at all. He is a good ST so i would not call him petty or vindictive save for when it comes to Sidereals in Exalted &amp; Mages in WoD he seems to make them Overpowered NPC's because he likes them to much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you think nobody cares if you're alive, try missing a couple of payments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2890-walker-of-ebony-clouds","name":"Walker-of-Ebony-Clouds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T17:55:57-07:00","id":149876,"title":"","content":"Sidereals are the most fragile type of Exalted for their &quot;power level&quot;, but that doesn't really have anything to do with their Ox-Body except insofar as their Ox-Body is a a loose thematic nod to the convention. If you were trying to assess it on the basis of individual elements like that you might well end up mistakenly believing that Sidereals are the tankiest Exalted, thematically, because they can attune Starmetal armour for half what everyone else can and it has potent damage reduction. It's more that Sidereals are fragile for <i>other</i> reasons, and the Ox-Body thing is an easy thing to point to as an example, because the actual reasons are the result of complex interactions embedded in their charmset. (Talking about 1e here, obviously. 2e Sidereals weren't designed, they just happened.)<br /> <br /> The thing that makes Sidereals fragile is that Exalted has always been constructed on the basis that all offense is strong and thus you need to defend strongly against all offense, but although Sidereals do have strong defenses, they have big holes in their repertoire and need to scramble to cover their bases. There are a lot of important, fundamental parts of an &quot;Exalted build&quot; that Sidereals either don't have, or have in a single form that's saddled with awkward limitations, and when getting hit <i>once</i> is serious business, these are perilous, and they need to make the most of what they have while making it look awesome. That's what the &quot;Sidereals are flimsy&quot; deal is about.<br /> <br /> Obviously, in 3e, this won't work very well, since a lot of the changes 3e is making are designed to remove the pressures that make fighting as a Sid tricky, while at the same time requiring <i>everyone</i> to keep on their toes in combat. So I'm interested to see what they do with them there!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T20:08:30-07:00","id":149962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=87607#post87607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not every Sidereal is Ketchup Carjack sitting on his chair manipulating his minion. Iron Siaka just pound demon's faces directly instead of making other people do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't meant that she is efficient at it, or that she <i>should </i>be.<br /> <br /> She might only be effective at it because of a ridiculous amount of investment that Terrestrials and Lunars would laugh at.<br /> <br /> (Note the deliberate difference between &quot;efficient&quot; and &quot;effective&quot;.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eh, shouldn't that mean they ought to get more HL per purchase instead of a single -0 level. </div> </div> </div>Buying one Charm pretty much <i>just</i> to offset the cost of another Charm (in a completely different tree, with a different Ability minimum) <i>does </i>seem to suck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T23:16:42-07:00","id":150062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=149962#post149962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't meant that she is efficient at it, or that she <i>should </i>be.<br /> <br /> She might only be effective at it because of a ridiculous amount of investment that Terrestrials and Lunars would laugh at.<br /> <br /> (Note the deliberate difference between &quot;efficient&quot; and &quot;effective&quot;.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's bullshit and you know it. Even with the pretty bad charmset that sidereals have it's still better than what terrestrials have even without dipping into MA. Depending on what her artifact can do anyway it's possible for her to compete with some Lunar builds. However, because of the limited nature of the charmset she'd have to use MA to compete with lunars. However, that's a closed charmset issue not a sidereal combat charms versus others issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T02:24:58-07:00","id":150145,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm not sure my intent was clear so i'll clarify :<br /> <br /> The idea is not about complaining about this or that, but to point out a fact and a (possible) solution if people think it's a problem.<br /> <br /> Namely, having a charm work exactly the same way for different exalts but each has access to different options, just as solars have the same OBT than sids except they have access to more options.<br /> The consequence is the solar version is STRICTLY better.<br /> <br /> One solution is to add a bonus different for each splat, especially since OBT are considered &quot;weak&quot; for their XP cost. The consequence is, while solar OBT is still arguably better (because the splat bonus should be balanced and they still have access to more options) it's not strictly better anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now in terms of &quot;tankiness&quot; sidereals were in fact not so bad in 2E. You could still stack armor with the resplendency that gave you +9B/+9L soak, Optimistic security practice, sidereal shell-games (with the advantage of reducing your enemy's), possibly medicine's pinacle charm. All of that without counting as wearing an armor.<br /> <br /> One of them main problems in this matter, just like in a lot of others, is that quite a few of their weaknesses were meant to be &quot;fixed&quot; by elements... that were not exclusive to them :<br /> - They have almost no access to hardness, but this is made up by starmetal armor bonus... that everyone can use<br /> - They have very few damage boosting charms, once again compensated by weapon MM bonus, and MA charms that raise minimum damage<br /> - They have arguably weaker combat charms, but they get access to SMA and a very powerful CMA... but solars have access too (and are even better at it because of their higher dice caps)<br /> <br /> The other elements that force them to &quot;glass canon&quot; style are :<br /> - the lack of DV boosting charms, especially since their MA style is a full-offense assassination-centered one<br /> - they are even more binary that other exalts.<br /> Duck fate : either you roll enough successes and you perfectly dodge, or you wasted 10 motes for strictly no bonus (and that was still when other perfects were at 3/5 motes).<br /> Walking outside fate and 2E optimistic security practice : both automatically succeed or fail depending on the enemy essence rating.<br /> Someone else's destiny 2E : You can perfectly ignore and redirect any poison (roll is trivial) but you once you have one dose &quot;stored&quot;, the charm is powerless until you hit and apply it to someone.<br /> Impending the flow 2E : Either the attack is perfect or unblockable and the charm has strictly no effect, or he perfectly negate the attack<br /> <br /> It's not always bad, but giving the option for different styles would be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T12:06:38-07:00","id":150674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=150062#post150062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's bullshit and you know it. Even with the pretty bad charmset that sidereals have it's still better than what terrestrials have even without dipping into MA. Depending on what her artifact can do anyway it's possible for her to compete with some Lunar builds. However, because of the limited nature of the charmset she'd have to use MA to compete with lunars. However, that's a closed charmset issue not a sidereal combat charms versus others issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>She's a <i>Chosen of Serenity</i>. Aside from Defense in Shining Joy and the actual Dodge Charms, she's <i>already </i>the poster-child for &quot;suboptimal builds&quot;.<br /> <br /> She just doesn't give a fuck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T12:30:04-07:00","id":150708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=149962#post149962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Buying one Charm pretty much <i>just</i> to offset the cost of another Charm (in a completely different tree, with a different Ability minimum) <i>does </i>seem to suck.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, for one, was never a fan of the idea that Ox-Bodies were meant to be mote pool expansion equivalents. For starters, it takes a lot longer for a health level to heal than motes to regenerate. And secondly, usually when you get hit with a weapon, you don't stand to loose between 1/7 and 1/12 of the resource you use to fuel your charms. When you do, you can usually stunt it back without too much difficulty. I sort of hope this is something that changes in 3e. But we'll see. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T12:36:47-07:00","id":150716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=150674#post150674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's a <i>Chosen of Serenity</i>. Aside from Defense in Shining Joy and the actual Dodge Charms, she's <i>already </i>the poster-child for &quot;suboptimal builds&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Chosen of Serenity get one of the most powerful tricks in the entire game.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Sidereals in 2.0 in general, I'm not too keen on their chances without Martial Arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","user":"emeraldstreak","date":". 05-27-2014, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T13:10:12-07:00","id":150742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/87572-sidereal-as-the-0-resistance-stamina-exalted?p=150674#post150674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's a <i>Chosen of Serenity</i>. Aside from Defense in Shining Joy and the actual Dodge Charms, she's <i>already </i>the poster-child for &quot;suboptimal builds&quot;.<br /> <br /> She just doesn't give a fuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>She's got one Caste ability that helps her fight and four favoured, that's on a par with what a Twilight or an Eclipse caste gets.<br /> <br /> Iron Siaka isn't that nonconformist mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 05-27-2014, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}